1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,212
Learning a Language: Where to Start.

2
00:00:03,162 --> 00:00:10,387
The key to language learning is comprehensible input: reading and listening to material slightly above the learner’s current level.

3
00:00:10,387 --> 00:00:15,950
Most of the content should be understandable, with a few new elements to absorb from context.

4
00:00:15,950 --> 00:00:20,612
Grammar study and vocabulary drilling are supplements, not the main event.

5
00:00:20,612 --> 00:00:23,575
Consistency matters more than intensity.

6
00:00:23,575 --> 00:00:27,337
Thirty minutes daily beats three hours once a week.

7
00:00:27,337 --> 00:00:33,125
Finding genuinely enjoyable content in the target language makes motivation self-sustaining.

8
00:00:33,125 --> 00:00:39,687
Speaking and writing are important but work best after building a foundation through extensive listening and reading.

